    "content": ":::section layout=\"image-above\" image=\"/assets/Media%20Monitoring_Approved%20Images/Media%20Monitoring_Set%20the%20Watchlist.png\" alt=\"A monitoring radar identifying relevant signals\"\n## A Mention Is Only the Starting Point\n\nMedia monitoring should not stop at counting articles, broadcasts or online references. Teams need to understand who is shaping the conversation, what has changed and how the story may develop next.\n\nTen neutral mentions in low-relevance outlets can matter less than one inaccurate report in a publication trusted by the audience that matters most.\n:::\n\n:::section layout=\"image-right\" image=\"/assets/Media%20Monitoring_Approved%20Images/Media%20Monitoring_Read%20What%20Changed.jpg\" alt=\"A team reading changes in media coverage\"\n## Read the Direction of the Story\n\nUseful monitoring considers several signals together:\n\n- the credibility and reach of the source;\n- the accuracy and tone of the coverage;\n- the narratives gaining momentum;\n- the people or outlets influencing the discussion;\n- the likelihood that the story will travel further.\n\nThis context separates background noise from issues that require attention.\n:::\n\n:::section layout=\"text\"\n## Decide Whether Action Helps\n\nNot every negative mention needs a response. Sometimes direct engagement adds unnecessary visibility. In other cases, an early clarification can prevent an incomplete claim from becoming the accepted version of events.\n\nThe decision should be based on the facts, the risk and the direction of the conversation—not on sentiment alone.\n:::\n\n:::section layout=\"image-left\" image=\"/assets/Media%20Monitoring_Approved%20Images/Media%20Monitoring_Act%20While%20It%20Matter.jpg\" alt=\"A communications team acting while a story is developing\"\n## Connect Monitoring to Response\n\nMonitoring creates value when it leads to a clear next move. That may mean preparing a spokesperson, correcting a factual error, briefing internal teams or continuing to watch the issue without public engagement.\n\n**The objective is not to react to everything. It is to act while the right action can still make a difference.**\n:::"
